                <pb facs="0294" n="196" xml:id="pg196"/>

                <head>PROTOCOL</head>
                <p>At the moment of signing the Convention of even date relating to the trade in
                    arms and ammunition, the undersigned Plenipotentiaries declare in the name of
                    their respective Governments that they would regard it as contrary to the
                    intention of the High Contracting Parties and to the spirit of this Convention
                    that, pending the coming into force of the Convention, a Contracting Party
                    should adopt any measure which is contrary to its provisions.</p>
                <closer>
